<SiteLayout title="File Conversion Guides | ConvertAnyFile" description="Practical guides to image and data formats, compatibility, compression, quality, HEIC, WebP, AVIF, JPG, PNG, CSV, JSON and choosing the right conversion workflow.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="site-container hero-inner"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Guides</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Conversion guides</span><h1>Understand the format before you convert it.</h1><p>Practical explanations for choosing outputs, avoiding quality myths, understanding compatibility, and deciding when conversion is actually useful.</p></div></section>

<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Why these guides exist</span><h2>Good conversion starts with the destination.</h2><p>A converter can change a file extension in seconds, but the right output depends on the image or data structure, compatibility requirements, editing workflow, and acceptable file size. These guides explain those trade-offs before you click Convert.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>People-first content</strong><p>Each guide is tied directly to a real conversion decision on ConvertAnyFile. The goal is useful format education, not pages created only to repeat keywords.</p></div></div></div></section>

<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Current guides</span><h2>Start with the question you are trying to solve.</h2><p>Format comparisons, phone compatibility, compression behavior, and structured-data choices are covered because they answer practical conversion decisions.</p></div><div class="category-grid">{guides.map((guide)=><a class="category-card category-card--live" href={guide.href}><div class="category-icon">G</div><div><span class="live-badge">Guide</span><h3>{guide.title}</h3><p>{guide.text}</p></div><span class="category-arrow">→</span></a>)}</div></div></section>

<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Practical path</span><h2>If you are not sure where to start.</h2></div><div class="comparison-table-wrap"><table class="comparison-table"><thead><tr><th>Your question</th><th>Best starting guide</th><th>Useful tool</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Should I use JPG or PNG?</td><td><a href="/guides/jpg-vs-png/">JPG vs PNG</a></td><td><a href="/png-to-jpg/">PNG to JPG</a></td></tr><tr><td>Should I use WebP or JPG?</td><td><a href="/guides/webp-vs-jpg/">WebP vs JPG</a></td><td><a href="/webp-to-jpg/">WebP to JPG</a></td></tr><tr><td>Should my website use WebP or AVIF?</td><td><a href="/guides/webp-vs-avif/">WebP vs AVIF</a></td><td><a href="/png-to-webp/">PNG to WebP</a></td></tr><tr><td>Why can nobody open my phone photo?</td><td><a href="/guides/heic-explained/">HEIC explained</a></td><td><a href="/heic-to-jpg/">HEIC to JPG</a></td></tr><tr><td>How do I convert HEIC photos to JPG?</td><td><a href="/guides/how-to-convert-heic-to-jpg/">HEIC to JPG how-to</a></td><td><a href="/heic-to-jpg/">HEIC to JPG</a></td></tr><tr><td>Should I use CSV or JSON?</td><td><a href="/guides/csv-vs-json/">CSV vs JSON</a></td><td><a href="/csv-to-json/">CSV to JSON</a></td></tr><tr><td>What does the Quality slider really do?</td><td><a href="/guides/image-quality-compression/">Image quality & compression</a></td><td><a href="/image-converter/">Image Converter</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>
